Importing `GateMode` inside the `run` method on every forward pass introduces unnecessary overhead in the hot path. Since `AiterRunnerCore` is instantiated once per MoE layer, we can cache the imported `GateMode` class on `self` to completely avoid this overhead on subsequent calls.

```suggestion
        if not hasattr(self, "_gate_mode_class"):
            try:
                from aiter.ops.flydsl.moe_common import GateMode
                self._gate_mode_class = GateMode
            except ImportError:
                self._gate_mode_class = None

        if self._gate_mode_class is not None:
            extra["gate_mode"] = (
                self._gate_mode_class.INTERLEAVE.value
                if envs.SGLANG_USE_AITER_MOE_GU_ITLV.get()
                else self._gate_mode_class.SEPARATED.value
            )
```

